hD Regulations\nContacts\nQuality Assurance\nPrivate Area\nMaster\nMaster in Trattamenti di Superficie per l'industria\nComunicazione delle Scienze\nStage\nTesine finali\nRegolamento\nStruttura\nCorsi\nDocenti\nSegreteria\nCondizioni per l'ammissione\nTestimonianze\nAttivit\u00e0 formative\nCosa dicono di noi\nCorsi di Alta Formazione\nCorso di Alta Formazione sulla Gestione ottica del Cheratocono\nCorso di Alta Formazione in Contattologia\nCorso di Alta Formazione in Gestione della Progressione Miopica\nScuola di specializzazione in Fisica medica\nAmmissione\nOrganizzazione\nConsiglio della Scuola\nCommissione didattica\nPolitica per la qualit\u00e0\nNormativa e Regolamento\nDidattica\nMissioni\nDiploma\nIniziative\nArchivio\nScuola Galileiana\nSummer e Winter Schools\nInclusione e Disabilit\u00e0\nPercorsi abilitanti per insegnanti\nBandi per insegnamenti\nSkip to content\nAcademic Year 2026/2027\nApplications for the next cycle XLII are now open. Further details are available on the University webpage: Italian version or English version\nDeadline: May 20, 2026, 1 p.m.\n7 POSITIONS AVAILABLE, STARTING ON NOVEMBER 1, 2026\n1) Four open positions funded by the University of Padova\nAt this web page you can find possible PhD thesis topics for the open positions. These proposed projects may be discussed during the oral examination, but they are not necessarily intended to be the final PhD projects. The final topic will be defined by the Board of Professors in agreement with the selected candidate. Applicants are encouraged to contact staff members of the DFA and INAF-OAPD to discuss potential PhD research topics.\n2) Three positions funded by INAF\nThese three INAF scholarships are thematic. Candidates must indicate their interest in applying for them within the application. The most deserving candidate who has selected one of these scholarships will be awarded it.\n1. Exploring the Universe with cutting-edge observations and/or simulations\n2. Frontiers of Astrophysics: studies of celestial bodies and astrophysical phenomena in research areas led by the INAF\u2013Astronomical Observatory of Padova\n3. Physical properties of AGNs at the Reionization Epoch and Cosmic Dawn (Project RECAP, ERC Synergy Grant \u2013 Grant Agreement No. 101166930, CUP No. C83C25000120006)\nRecipients of the first and second INAF scholarships will be required, at a later stage, to choose one of the projects listed in the attached file.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdmission procedure\nAdmission is based on the evaluation of the candidate\u2019s CV and an oral examination. Candidates are strongly encouraged to use the provided their CV template.\nIn addition to the CV, applicants must submit a brief description (maximum one page) of a research project of their interest.\nThis research proposal should outline the state of the art, the objectives, and the methodology, regardless of the chosen topic.\nThe PhD topics listed on the webpage may be discussed during the oral examination but are not binding as final research projects. The final topic will be defined by the Board of Professors in agreement with the successful candidate.\nLetters of recommendation are not required.\nThe oral examination will include both a discussion of the proposed research project and an assessment of the candidate\u2019s general background in astronomy.\nA list of general topics for the oral exam is available on the webpage.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe only official and legally binding source is the original Italian announcement available at https://www.unipd.it/dottorato/dottorati-42-ciclo\nDetails about the selection (ITA) - (ENG)\nFor further information:\nAdministrative office:\ndott. ssa ALESSANDRA ZORZI\nE-mail: alessandra.zorzi(at)unipd(dot)it - didattica.dfa(at)unipd(dot)it\nTel: 049-827.8261\nCoordinator of Doctoral Course in Astronomy:\nProf. GIOVANNI CARRARO\nE-mail: giovanni.carraro(at)unipd(dot)it\nTel: 049-827.8230\nDIPARTIMENTO DI FISICA E ASTRONOMIA \"GALILEO GALILEI\"\nAmministrazione trasparente\nPersone\nCONTATTI\nVia F. Marzolo, 8 - 35131 Padova\nTelefono: +39 049 827 7088\nFax: +39 049 827 7102\nPec: dipartimento.dfa(at)pec.unipd.it\nSegnalazioni al webmaster: webmaster(at)dfa.unipd.it\n\u00a9 2018 Universit\u00e0 di Padova - Tutti i diritti riservati\nP.I. 00742430283 C.F. 80006480281\nInformazioni sul sito\n|\nAccessibilit\u00e0\n|\nPrivacy", "links": [["Vai al contenuto", "http://www.dfa.unipd.it/didattica/dottorati-di-ricerca/phd-in-astronomy/admission/academic-year-20262027/#main"], ["Uniweb", "https://uniweb.unipd.it/"], ["Unipd", "http://www.unipd.it"], ["Dipartimenti", "http://www.unipd.it/dipartimenti"], ["Scuole", "https://www.unipd.it/scuole"], ["Biblioteche", "http://www.unipd.it/biblioteche"], ["Webmail", "https://www.unipd.it/webmail"], ["SIT", "https://www.unipd.it/sit"], ["GeBeS PTA", "https://apex.cca.unipd.it/pls/apex/f?p=1300:1:114307609289822::NO:1:P0_FSVM_COD_ID,P0_FSVM_NUM_RIG,P0_FSDG_APPP_COD_ID,P0_FSVM_NUM_RIG_MENU_L2,P0_AZIONE,P0_FSNE_COD_NEWS_ID,P0_FSDO_COD_DOC_ID,P0_FSAF_COD_APE_FUN,P0_FSVM_DES_VOCE_MENU,P0_PAGE:925,,54048,,,,,,Home,1"], ["Rubrica", "https://www.unipd.it/rubrica"], ["", "http://www.dfa.unipd.it/"], ["CERCA", "javascript:void(0)"], ["Menu", "javascript:void(0)"], ["ENG", "http://www.dfa.unipd.it/en/"], ["CHIUDI", "javascript:void(0)"], ["Dipartimento", "javascript:void(0)"], ["Salta al menu-{field:uid}", "http://www.dfa.unipd.it/didattica/dottorati-di-ricerca/phd-in-astronomy/admission/academic-year-20262027/#menu-{field:uid}"], ["Presentazione", "http://www.dfa.unipd.it/didattica/dottorati-di-ricerca/phd-in-astronomy/admission/academic-year-20262027/dipartimento/presentazione/"], ["Organigramma", "http://www.dfa.unipd.it/didattica/dottorati-di-ricerca/phd-